-- title:
--   Finite group action on X_H(q²M') with invariants the Γ₀-field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))/L$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb Q \to L$, of the rational $q$-expansion field attached to $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the series $\mathsf q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`, under the coefficient embedding. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field equal to the base change to $L$ of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $j(\mathsf q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $q^2M'$, and assume $K_2 \le K$. Then there exist a type $G$ with a group structure, a finiteness structure on $G$, and an action of $G$ on $K$ by ring automorphisms fixing nothing prescribed a priori, such that, for the $K_2$-algebra structure on $K$ coming from the inclusion $K_2 \le K$: the $G$-action commutes with multiplication by elements of $K_2$ and $K$ is $G$-invariant over $K_2$ in the sense that the $G$-fixed elements of $K$ are exactly those coming from $K_2$; the $G$-action commutes with multiplication by elements of $L$; the action is faithful; and $g \cdot j = j$ for every $g \in G$.
--
--   This packages the action of the diamond operators, i.e. of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')/\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, on the covering $X_H(q^2M') \to X_0(q^2M')$ in the form of a finite group of ring automorphisms of the base-changed function field whose invariant subfield is the $\Gamma_0$-level field and which fixes the $j$-invariant. It is used in the analysis of the fibres of $X_H(q^2M') \to X_0(q^2M')$ near the cusp, in particular in the study of minimal primes over the ideal generated by the $j$-invariant chart at infinity and of the induced action on the charts.
